# Run the app only when debugging

Routine UI, layout, styling, routing, and component work ends when the code is written.
Do not start the backend/frontend, open a browser, take screenshots, or run Playwright
as a post-edit checklist.

Start the app (`run-app`) and use the browser (`ui-verify`, Playwright, chrome-devtools)
only when:

- the user asked to run / open / verify the app, or
- you are debugging a live issue that cannot be diagnosed from code, logs, or types.

If the servers are already running, reuse them. Do not restart them to "verify" an edit.
